---
import { renderToString } from "katex";
import type { Mode } from "../lib/site-data";
interface Props { mode: Mode }
const { mode } = Astro.props;
const expert = mode === "expert";
const math = (s: string) => renderToString(s, { displayMode: true, output: "htmlAndMathml", throwOnError: true });
---
<section class="mass-ledger luong-operations" aria-labelledby="luong-support-heading">
  <header class="ledger-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Source operations · symbolic rules</p><h2 id="luong-support-heading">Which positions can contribute?</h2></div><p class="ledger-folio">Global / local<br />§3.1–3.2</p></header>
  <div class="trace-intro"><p>These are symbolic source rules, not learned alignments or a translation trace. S is source length; t is the target step; D is the window half-width.</p>
    <section class="luong-support-rule"><h3>Fixed summary · no new positional read</h3><p>The earlier chapters retain one source summary for the target sequence. The decoder still depends on the source through that summary; it makes no new selection over individual source positions at each step.</p><p class="luong-rule">One source summary → target sequence</p></section>
    <section class="luong-support-rule"><h3>Global · every source position</h3><p>For a content-based global read, compare the current decoder state with every source state. Normalize across that source support, then sum the weighted states. The fixed-length location variant has a separate boundary below.</p><p class="luong-rule">All valid s → content weights → context</p></section>
    <section class="luong-support-rule"><h3>Local-m · center follows the target step</h3><p>Set pₜ = t. Restrict the read to the source window [t − D, t + D], dropping its part outside the sentence. Approximate monotonicity is an assumption.</p><p class="luong-rule">Before window: excluded · inside: eligible · after: excluded</p></section>
    <section class="luong-support-rule"><h3>Local-p · predict the center</h3><p>Predict a real pₜ from hₜ and S. Within its neighborhood, multiply content alignment weights by a Gaussian favoring positions near pₜ. The center can change with the decoder state; it need not advance monotonically.</p><p class="luong-rule">Predict pₜ → local content alignment → Gaussian multiplication</p></section>
    <p class="provenance-note mt-3">A source position outside a local window cannot directly contribute its state to that step’s context. Neither a large weight nor the predicted center certifies a translated word. The local window is not a user-selected coverage mask.</p>
    <details class="prediction-reveal mt-4"><summary>{expert ? "Audit support and the normalization claim" : "Check what a window can miss"}</summary><p>{expert ? "Global content softmax sums to one over its source support. Local-m uses the restricted window. For local-p, multiplying normalized content weights by the printed Gaussian does not itself preserve that sum. The paper prints no final renormalization. Do not silently apply the global invariant after the multiplier." : "A word can matter to the translation yet lie outside the chosen neighborhood. Its source state is then excluded from this context. Moving the center can change eligibility; it does not guarantee a correct alignment or translation."}</p></details>
    {expert && <div class="equation-panel mt-4" role="region" aria-label="Luong local source operations with version-specific equation numbers" tabindex="0"><div set:html={math(String.raw`p_t=S\,\sigma\!\left(v_p^\top\tanh(W_ph_t)\right),\quad \sigma_{\mathrm{window}}=D/2`)} /><div set:html={math(String.raw`a_t(s)=\operatorname{align}(h_t,\bar h_s)\exp\!\left(-\frac{(s-p_t)^2}{2\sigma_{\mathrm{window}}^2}\right)`)} /><p>Proceedings Eqs. 10–11; arXiv v5 Eqs. 9–10. Here σ(·) denotes sigmoid; σ<sub>window</sub> names the paper’s Gaussian standard deviation to avoid conflating the two symbols.</p></div>}
    <details class="trace-arithmetic mt-4"><summary>Inspect the local-p source boundary</summary><dl class="alignment-version-list"><div><dt>What the text specifies</dt><dd>A real center, integer source positions in a surrounding window, σ = D/2, and ignoring the part outside the sentence. v5 calls the Gaussian truncated and qualifies differentiability to almost everywhere.</dd></div><div><dt>What is not calculated here</dt><dd>Integer support at center transitions, the precise denominator/selection order, final normalization and correspondence to the historical implementation have not been reconciled for a numerical fixture. No local-p weights or gradients are supplied.</dd></div><div><dt>Version boundary</dt><dd>The proceedings omits D; v5 specifies D = 10. That later value does not resolve the remaining conventions or establish what every earlier run used.</dd></div></dl></details>
  </div>
</section>
